<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.13.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00601</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.13.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2f2bd036-d7ef-4062-8a77-764f4208af4d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>This year, students
    in the 9th grade are collecting dimes and quarters for a school
    fundraiser. They are trying to collect more money than the students who were
    in the 9th grade last year. The students in 9th grade last year collected
    $143.88.</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Using \(d\) to represent the number of dimes collected and \(q\) to represent the number of quarters, which statement best
        represents this situation?</item>
</list>
    <list>
  <item> \( 0.25d+0.1q≥143.88 \)</item>
  <item> \( 0.25q+0.1d≥143.88 \)</item>
  <item> \( 0.25d+0.1q&gt;143.88 \)</item>
  <item> \( 0.25q+0.1d&gt;143.88 \)</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(0.25q+0.1d&gt;143.88 \)
</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which inequality is
        represented by the graph?</item>
</list>
    <para><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a coordinate plane, origin O. Each axis from negative 8 to 8, by 2’s. Dashed line goes through negative 2 comma negative 10, 0 comma negative 6, and 4 comma 2. The region below the dashed line is shaded."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a1cf2edc2ae294385d8b68efdd4025a752151ae3"/></media></figure></para>
    <list>
  <item>\( 4x−2y&gt;12 \)</item>
  <item> \( 4x−2y&lt;12 \)</item>
  <item> \( 4x+2y&gt;12 \)</item>
  <item> \( 4x+2y&lt;12 \)</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \( 4x−2y&lt;12 \)
</para>
    <para>For exercises 3-4, use the passage below to answer the
  questions:</para>
    <para><quote>A farmer is creating a budget  for planting soybeans and wheat. Planting
        soybeans costs $200 per acre and planting wheat costs $500 per acre. He wants
        to spend no more than $100,000 planting soybeans and wheat.</quote></para><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Let \(s\) represent the
        number of acres of soybeans and \(w\) represent the number of acres of wheat.
        Write an inequality to describe the situation.</item>
</list>
    <list>
  <item> \(500s + 200w &lt; 100,000\)</item>
  <item>\(    500s + 200w
        ≤ 100,000\)</item>
  <item>\(    200s + 500w
        ≤ 100,000\)</item>
  <item>\(    200s + 500w &gt; 100,000\)
      </item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \( 200s + 500w ≤ 100,000 \)</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> Name one solution to
        the inequality and explain what it represents in that situation.</item>
</list>
    <list>
  <item>\((200, 130)\)</item>
  <item>\((250, 100)\)</item>
  <item>\((170, 140)\)</item>
  <item>\(      (300, 90) \)</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((250, 100)\)</para>
    <para>For exercises 5-7, use the passage below to answer the
  questions:</para>
    <para><quote>Amira is ordering dried chili peppers and corn husks for
        her cooking class. Chili peppers cost $16.95 per pound and corn husks cost
        $6.49 per pound.</quote><quote>Amira spends less than $50 on \( d \)<emphasis effect="italics"> </emphasis>pounds of dried chili peppers and \( h \) pounds of corn husks.pounds of dried chili peppers and \( h \) pounds of corn husks.</quote><quote>Here is a graph that represents this
        situation.</quote><quote><figure><media alt="Inequality on grid"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a759f4aa3fb063072bdd2757468a7e1efcb84fb0"/></media></figure></quote></para><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write an
        inequality that represents this situation.</item>
</list>
    <list>
  <item>\(16.95d +
        6.49h ≥ 50\)</item>
  <item>\(16.95d –
        6.49h &lt; 50\)</item>
  <item>\(16.95d +
        6.49h &lt; 50\)</item>
  <item>\(16.95d +
        6.49h &gt; 50 \)</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \( 16.95d + 6.49h &lt; 50 \)</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Can Amira purchase 2 pounds of dried chili peppers and 4 pounds of corn husks
        and spend less than $50? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> No. She would be spending \( 16.95(2) + 6.49(4) \), or
  $59.86.</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Can Amira purchase 1.5 pounds of dried chili peppers and 3 pounds of corn
        husks and spend less than $50? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Yes. She would be spending \( 16.95(1.5) + 6.49(3) \), or $44.90.</para>
    <para>For exercises 8-10, use the passage below to answer the
  questions:</para>
    <para><quote>A beach store rents surfboards for $15
        per hour and beach umbrellas for $10 per hour. The store wants to make at least
        $200 per day on renting beach equipment. Let \( s \) be the number of hours that a surfboard is rented and \( u \) be the number of hours an umbrella is
        rented.</quote></para><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which inequality represents this situation?</item>
</list>
    <list>
  <item>\(15s – 10u ≥ 200\)</item>
  <item>\(15s + 10u ≤ 200\)</item>
  <item>\( 
        
        15s + 10u ≥ 200\)</item>
  <item>\(15s + 10u
        &lt; 200\) </item>
</list>
    <para><b>Answer: </b>\(15s + 10u ≥ 200\)</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Can the
        beach store rent surfboards for 7 total hours and rent umbrellas for 9
        total hours and reach their goal of making $200? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>No. They would be making \( 15(7) + 10(9) \), or $195.</para>
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Can the
        beach store rent surfboards for 10 total hours and rent umbrellas for 4
        total hours and reach their goal of making $200? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>No. They would be making \( 15(10) + 10(4) \), or $190.</para>
   <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
<item>Mariah has data in a table.   Use desmos to plot the data and find a possible inequality in two variables that could be represented by this data. Which graph represents this inequality?</item>
</list>

<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
<thead>
         <row>
           <entry><emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>\(y\)</emphasis></entry></row>
  </thead>
       <tbody>
         <row>
           <entry>−4</entry>
           <entry>7</entry>
         </row>
         <row>
           <entry>−2</entry>
           <entry>3</entry>
         </row>
         <row>
           <entry>0</entry>
           <entry>-1</entry>
         </row>
         <row>
           <entry>2</entry>
           <entry>-5</entry>
         </row>
       </tbody>
     </table>
<list>
  <item>\(y &lt; -2x-4\)</item>
  <item>\(y \leq -2x-4\)</item>
  <item>\(y &gt; -2x-4\)</item>
  <item>\(y \leq -2x-4\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(y &gt; -2x-4\)</para>


      
</section>
